.TH fmt_escapecharc 3
.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharc \- escape a character using C-style octal sequences
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
size_t \fBfmt_escapecharc\fR(char *\fIdest\fR, int \fIchr\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfmt_escapecharc\fR encodes the character \fIchr\fR into a C-style escaped representation.
.PP
If \fIchr\fR corresponds to a common escape sequence (e.g., '\n', '\t', '\e'), it is encoded as a 2-byte sequence (a backslash followed by the escape character). Otherwise, it is encoded as a 4-byte sequence: a backslash followed by three octal digits.
.PP
If \fIdest\fR is not NULL, the encoded character is written to \fIdest\fR.
.PP
The function returns the number of bytes required (or written) for the encoding. It returns 0 if \fIchr\fR > 0xff.
.SH SEE ALSO
fmt_escapecharcx(3), fmt_escapecharcontrol(3)